Each iteration of a loop body has its own scope, as in Jinja2: an assignment in the body lasts until its
iteration ends. Upstream ran every iteration in one scope, so a name set in one iteration was still set in the
next (GLM-5.3-Flash's template sets `reasoning_content` for one assistant message and tests `is defined` for
the next). The context records the iteration's assignments with the values they replaced and undoes them,
latest first, when the iteration ends, so an iteration costs its own assignments and never the scope's size.
